The same source, formatted at tab width 4 and 2 (see tab_width_2.txtar), must lay
out differently: a tab's column count decides where a line overflows. Nothing
pinned this before — changing pretty's tabWidth broke zero tests, which measured
coverage, not safety.

Indentation is emitted as tabs either way. tab_width changes only the measure.

Uses <div>, not <span>: since the fill-layout work, an inline atom (a
phrasing tag whose children are Text/Interp/atom, no forced break) renders
fully flat via atomDoc regardless of width — <span> here would no longer be
tab-width-sensitive. <div> is never an atom, so its own attr/children Group
still wraps under width pressure and the pair keeps pinning tabWidth's effect.

-- tab_width --
4
-- input.gsx --
package ui

component C() {
	<div>
		<section>
			<div class="aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa">x</div>
		</section>
	</div>
}
-- fmt.golden --
package ui

component C() {
	<div>
		<section>
			<div class="aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa">
				x
			</div>
		</section>
	</div>
}
